===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|abhor|ence}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/əbˈhɒɹ.n̩(t)s/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/æbˈhɔɹ.n̩(t)s/|/æbˈhɑɹ.n̩(t)s/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-abhorrence.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|countable}} Extreme [[aversion]] or [[detestation]]; the feeling of [[utter]] [[dislike]] or [[loathe|loathing]]. {{defdate|Mid 17<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=4}}</ref>
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1818|author=Mary Shelley|title=Frankenstein|chapter=9| url=http://ebooks.adelaide.edu.au/s/shelley/mary/s53f/chapter9.html| passage=My '''abhorrence''' of this [[fiend]] cannot be conceived.| archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120403120050/http://ebooks.adelaide.edu.au/s/shelley/mary/s53f/chapter9.html| archivedate=3 April 2012}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Numbers| volume=5| page=55| author=Dr. Philip J. Budd, ‎David Allen Hubbard, ‎Glenn W. Barker| year=2018| passage=The recognition of what pollutes evidently reflects deep-seated '''abhorrences''', whose cause and origin are difficult to discover.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|obsolete|historical}} An expression of abhorrence, in particular any of the parliamentary addresses dictated towards Charles II. {{defdate|Late 17<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[person]] or [[thing]] that is [[loathsome]]; a detested thing. {{defdate|Mid 18<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
#* {{quote-book|en|title=[Re]Gained in Translation I: Bibles, Theologies, and the Politics of Empowerment| page=276| author=Sabine Dievenkorn, ‎Shaul Levin| year=2022| passage=All of them are {{m|he|תובעות}} '''abhorrences''' or abominations, although “adultery and bestiality” are branded as “unclean” ({{m|he|אמט}}) activities. Because “homosexuality” is classified as one of the “'''abhorrences''',” Milgrom believes the practice was “widespread."| pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=tdqAEAAAQBAJ&pg=PA276&dq=%22abhorrences%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjFkPypwf6FAxXurokEHb2nDtAQ6AF6BAghEAI#v=onepage&q=%22abhorrences%22&f=false}}

